🔶 C) Mutation After Publish?

Right now:
	•	Publish Gate sets publish_eligible=true
	•	Then state becomes Published

But what if:
	•	Someone edits stage3_execution_plan.md afterward?
	•	Or edits escalations.md?

Your RESUME PRECHECK will detect mutation.

But do you allow re-opening a Published cycle?

You did not explicitly forbid it.

Right now, resume rules would:
	•	Detect mutation
	•	Invalidate downstream steps
	•	Re-run integrity checks

Which means a Published cycle could become non-Validated.

That may be desirable — but it should be intentional.

You may want:

If status == Published and mutation detected → require explicit --mode strict and confirm re-opening intent.

Otherwise cycles are not immutable.

